te_shrhldr_yield":0.02186288150400496,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":35.4,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.07079549244640308,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.06272,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":41.8,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Curbline Properties Corp. is the owner and manager of convenience shopping centers. It is positioned on the curbline of well-trafficked intersections and major vehicular corridors in suburban, high household income communities. The Company is a self-managed real estate investment trust (REIT) that is publicly traded under on the NYSE.Curbline Properties Corp. was incorporated on October 25th, 2023 in Maryland and is based in New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David R. Lukes | President, CEO & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $2.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 39 people. Revenue per employee of $4.7M ranks in the above the sector median among Real Estate peers. Stock-based compensation of $332K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Curbline Properties Corp. is a mid-cap real estate business with a $3.5B market cap on $183M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +51% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 2% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 4.3\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 6.3% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 368% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":3.679657590706898},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (24.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 268% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $36.8M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Growing faster than most Real Estate peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Curbline Properties Corp. (NYSE:CURB) Stock Has Average Price Target of $32.44","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/curbline-properties-corp-nysecurb-stock-has-average-price-target-of-32-44.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794392121.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Cu